# Agent build handover log

`AGENT-BUILD-UPDATES.md` at the repo root is the builder-to-architect handover. The architect agent reads it for what shipped, what gates passed, and what still needs human Xcode (only when device build failed or signing/capabilities block).

## When to write

Before you end a builder session, declare **MILESTONE COMPLETE**, or hand work to the architect, append a new dated section if you changed Swift, tests, scripts, or milestone acceptance state. Skip only for read-only questions with no repo changes.

## How to write

- Append at the **bottom** (newest last). Do not rewrite prior entries.
- Use `## YYYY-MM-DD — <milestone or topic>` as the heading.
- No em dashes, en dashes, or double dashes in the log (match Signal copy rules).

### Required subsections

| Section | Content |
|---------|---------|
| **Shipped** | Bullet list of user-visible or architectural outcomes |
| **Gate A (agent)** | `build_device` + `install_app` + `launch_app` (and watch install script if applicable); unit tests if milestone requires them. Pass/fail/not-run with reason. Use `build_sim`/`test_sim` only when noted as faster for that session. |
| **Gate B (human)** | Only steps the agent truly cannot run: signing blocked, device locked/offline, subjective gym feel (haptics/audio), or FM/HealthKit data the sim cannot fake. If device MCP succeeded, say "agent verified" and list any human-only spot checks. |
| **Human Xcode** | Only when `build_device` failed due to target membership, capabilities, or signing. Empty section if agent build passed. Never claim you edited pbxproj. |
| **Out of scope** | What you deliberately did not touch |
| **Files touched** | Table: Area \| Files |

### Optional subsections

- **Field report** if the human reported runtime symptoms and you diagnosed or fixed them
- **Follow-up fix** if you iterated after an initial ship

## Architect agent

On starting architecture or handoff work, read `AGENT-BUILD-UPDATES.md` from the latest `##` entry downward. Treat that as ground truth over chat memory for recent builder output.

## Do not use for

- Milestone task specs stay in `HANDOFF-*.md` / `M4-AGENT-HANDOFF.md` (architect to builder). Do not duplicate full handoff prompts into the build log.
- Long design history belongs in `build-a-very-detailed-foamy-pixel.md`, not this log.
